1
00:00:07,746 --> 00:00:11,817
[Subtitles by danielsangeo]

2
00:00:12,484 --> 00:00:14,853
I'm wasting my damned time.

3
00:00:14,853 --> 00:00:19,958
I'm trying to open this elevator, but I'm
90% sure this elevator only goes down,

4
00:00:19,958 --> 00:00:21,426
like everything else here.

5
00:00:21,426 --> 00:00:23,228
That's pretty far down, though.

6
00:00:23,228 --> 00:00:25,664
All this security must be
protect something.

7
00:00:25,664 --> 00:00:28,967
I bet we have gnomes down there
mining precious metals and gems.

8
00:00:28,967 --> 00:00:29,835
I want a gnome.

9
00:00:30,702 --> 00:00:32,070
Damn, there's another alien.

10
00:00:33,972 --> 00:00:37,709
I'd put my gnome in a cage and feed
him granola.  I think they'd eat that.

11
00:00:37,709 --> 00:00:38,810
Eh, who am I kidding?

12
00:00:38,810 --> 00:00:41,713
If the aliens got down there, they'd
have eaten them all by now anyway.

13
00:00:41,713 --> 00:00:42,981
Gnomes are small.

14
00:00:42,981 --> 00:00:44,516
Wait, are gnomes even real?

15
00:00:44,516 --> 00:00:45,650
[headcrab squeals]
I can't re--WHOA!

16
00:00:47,152 --> 00:00:48,954
Dammit, I'm being followed again.

17
00:00:49,254 --> 00:00:52,824
What happened to that soldier guy?
I thought he was taking care of this?

18
00:00:52,824 --> 00:00:54,893
Nobody's doing their job.

19
00:00:54,893 --> 00:00:57,829
Why is everyone who's
not me such a problem?

20
00:00:57,829 --> 00:01:01,166
Y'know, some people might argue
I'm only focusing on the negative,

21
00:01:01,166 --> 00:01:03,835
but I think that's because I
can't think of one thing today

22
00:01:03,835 --> 00:01:05,637
anyone else has done right.

23
00:01:05,637 --> 00:01:08,306
All anyone has been doing today
has been breaking things,

24
00:01:08,306 --> 00:01:09,708
running around screaming,

25
00:01:09,708 --> 00:01:11,076
shooting the wrong people,

26
00:01:11,076 --> 00:01:12,110
or dying.

27
00:01:12,110 --> 00:01:14,179
I mean, what am I
supposed to say to people?

28
00:01:14,179 --> 00:01:17,749
"Wow, you sure did a good job
falling down that elevator shaft!"

29
00:01:17,749 --> 00:01:21,920
Or "Way to lock yourself inside
the freezer.  I'm so proud of you."

30
00:01:22,487 --> 00:01:24,856
Hey, this is the homeless guy's foundation.

31
00:01:24,856 --> 00:01:26,925
I'm going in circles again!

32
00:01:26,925 --> 00:01:28,393
I'd better speed up.

33
00:01:28,393 --> 00:01:30,729
If going to go in circles,
I want to go faster.

34
00:01:31,396 --> 00:01:33,398
Wait, wait wait, wait, wait.

35
00:01:33,398 --> 00:01:37,736
I haven't checked this tunnel out, and
I'm still waiting for hidden treasure.

36
00:01:37,736 --> 00:01:40,205
We get funding for
a lot of shady projects.

37
00:01:40,205 --> 00:01:42,507
Maybe there's some Nazi gold back here.

38
00:01:42,507 --> 00:01:44,509
Siegen sie mir das geld.

39
00:01:44,509 --> 00:01:46,044
Eh, there's nothing here.

40
00:01:46,044 --> 00:01:48,480
Just a dead end and some more boxes.

41
00:01:48,480 --> 00:01:51,416
Probably filled with
network cards we can't use.

42
00:01:51,416 --> 00:01:53,251
BNC or something.

43
00:01:53,251 --> 00:01:55,220
Well, back on the labyrinth ride.

44
00:01:55,220 --> 00:01:57,255
See, I'm remaining calm
about going in circles

45
00:01:57,255 --> 00:02:00,992
because I know I haven't investigated
every possible path yet.

46
00:02:00,992 --> 00:02:03,361
See, there's one.
I don't know where that goes.

47
00:02:03,361 --> 00:02:05,864
Some people stay lost their
WHOLE LIVES!

48
00:02:06,531 --> 00:02:06,898
Eeeh...

49
00:02:07,499 --> 00:02:08,433
In fact, most people.

50
00:02:08,967 --> 00:02:09,567
EVERYONE!

51
00:02:09,968 --> 00:02:12,170
Everyone's lost, except me.

52
00:02:12,170 --> 00:02:13,471
Except for right now.

53
00:02:13,872 --> 00:02:14,806
There's that hook again.

54
00:02:14,806 --> 00:02:17,242
I'm going to come back here
if I can't find the right way.

55
00:02:17,242 --> 00:02:21,279
I won't be surprised if this entire track
is devoted to taking people in circles,

56
00:02:21,279 --> 00:02:22,514
but I will be disappointed.

57
00:02:23,014 --> 00:02:25,684
Hey, there's one of those signs
again that might do something.

58
00:02:26,251 --> 00:02:27,018
I'm going to shoot it.

59
00:02:28,019 --> 00:02:30,622
That's so weird; it spins the wrong way.

60
00:02:30,622 --> 00:02:35,393
Now, did that actually do anything, or am
I shooting at things for no reason again?

61
00:02:35,393 --> 00:02:37,629
Ah!  It did!

62
00:02:37,629 --> 00:02:38,730
I'm surprised that worked.

63
00:02:38,730 --> 00:02:42,000
I wouldn't have thought that shooting
road signs was the correct thing to do.

64
00:02:42,000 --> 00:02:43,101
[rumbling]
I always thought that--

65
00:02:43,101 --> 00:02:47,205
Jesus Christ, are we running a
geothermal plant down here, too?

66
00:02:47,205 --> 00:02:48,106
Stop, stop.

67
00:02:48,673 --> 00:02:51,910
Okay, a dead body and an
alien who hasn't seen me yet.

68
00:02:51,910 --> 00:02:54,045
I can put one and one together.

69
00:02:54,846 --> 00:02:56,681
Actually, that's one and negative one.

70
00:02:57,849 --> 00:02:59,851
Now it's negative two and me.

71
00:03:00,285 --> 00:03:02,287
But wait, wouldn't I be number one?

72
00:03:02,754 --> 00:03:04,656
I don't know what
the hell I'm talking about.

73
00:03:04,656 --> 00:03:06,758
See, this is why you
have to define your terms.

74
00:03:06,758 --> 00:03:08,326
If you don't, people die.

75
00:03:08,693 --> 00:03:10,795
Oop, there's that tentacle again.

76
00:03:12,030 --> 00:03:13,665
Bad spot, chunky.

77
00:03:14,199 --> 00:03:16,034
Get it all up, I'll wait.

78
00:03:16,601 --> 00:03:19,771
I should've just driven the tram
straight through it, but, I dunno,

79
00:03:19,771 --> 00:03:22,173
that might've caused it to come
crashing down on top of me.

80
00:03:22,607 --> 00:03:23,942
Wouldn't want that.

81
00:03:24,509 --> 00:03:27,345
I wonder if circus people
already know about these things.

82
00:03:27,345 --> 00:03:28,580
Carnies.

83
00:03:28,580 --> 00:03:32,150
Some of the strangest things I've ever seen
in my life have been at the freak show.

84
00:03:32,150 --> 00:03:36,354
Ah, but they had the freaks in
cages where they belong!

85
00:03:37,222 --> 00:03:39,958
Back.  There might be something here.

86
00:03:39,958 --> 00:03:41,459
Besides death, I mean.

87
00:03:41,459 --> 00:03:42,527
I doubt there will be.

88
00:03:42,894 --> 00:03:45,730
I'm sure I'll go up the stairs and
find nothing but a stack of dead bodies,

89
00:03:45,730 --> 00:03:46,998
with a smiley-faced sticker attached--

90
00:03:46,998 --> 00:03:47,632
[headcrab squeals]
with a smiley-faced sticker attached--

91
00:03:47,632 --> 00:03:48,299
Fugh!

92
00:03:50,635 --> 00:03:51,870
That was sneaky!

93
00:03:53,338 --> 00:03:54,472
Where did you go?!

94
00:03:56,441 --> 00:03:58,476
Well, let that be a lesson to you.

95
00:03:59,010 --> 00:04:02,981
How did those bastards know to jump towards
the only vulnerable part of my body?

96
00:04:02,981 --> 00:04:06,084
If I was quick enough, I might be able
to headbutt them, but I don't--

97
00:04:06,084 --> 00:04:08,453
Now, what's this?  The sentry gun?

98
00:04:08,453 --> 00:04:10,855
It can't be bothered to shoot
those aliens crawling around,

99
00:04:10,855 --> 00:04:13,758
yet it has no problems
seeing me through a wall?

100
00:04:14,259 --> 00:04:16,828
These things cause more
problems than they solve.

101
00:04:17,262 --> 00:04:18,897
Ah-hah!  Buttons!

102
00:04:19,130 --> 00:04:20,131
What did that do?

103
00:04:20,565 --> 00:04:21,733
Oh, it moved the hook.

104
00:04:22,100 --> 00:04:24,569
So, why the hell was
that there in the first place?

105
00:04:24,569 --> 00:04:26,104
Well, that opens up some options.

106
00:04:26,104 --> 00:04:29,941
And I'm going to be Mr. Efficiency
and switch the track while I'm up here.

107
00:04:29,941 --> 00:04:32,944
Because maybe I'm just a pessimist,

108
00:04:32,944 --> 00:04:35,847
but I get the sneaking sensation
this track is going to find a way

109
00:04:35,847 --> 00:04:37,649
to send me back in circles again.

110
00:04:37,649 --> 00:04:40,685
I mean, why should it be any different
than anything else in this building?

111
00:04:40,685 --> 00:04:43,488
I don't think this tram
has any real function here.

112
00:04:43,488 --> 00:04:45,857
It's just some CEO's fantasy track.

113
00:04:45,857 --> 00:04:47,792
Why have a model train
that goes in circles

114
00:04:47,792 --> 00:04:49,527
when you can afford the real thing?

115
00:04:49,928 --> 00:04:50,662
Aah!

116
00:04:53,231 --> 00:04:57,402
Yeah, I'm sure before long, I'll start
seeing some giant Styrofoam trees.

117
00:04:57,402 --> 00:05:00,972
I will say that I do dig this
sign-shooting track switch system.

118
00:05:00,972 --> 00:05:03,975
I mean, I thought there'd be a
control station with--Ah, wire!

119
00:05:03,975 --> 00:05:05,710
I AM going in circles.

120
00:05:05,710 --> 00:05:08,146
But no, they just want
you to shoot the signs.

121
00:05:08,146 --> 00:05:11,616
Like drunk hillbillies shooting
deer-crossing signs from their pickups.

122
00:05:11,616 --> 00:05:12,517
Works for me.

123
00:05:12,517 --> 00:05:13,451
[imitating banjo plucking]

124
00:05:13,451 --> 00:05:14,352
[machine gun fire]
[imitating banjo plucking]

125
00:05:14,352 --> 00:05:15,520
Hm.  Gunfire.

126
00:05:15,520 --> 00:05:18,089
I've changed my stance
from that being a happy thing.

127
00:05:18,089 --> 00:05:20,525
HEY, DON'T MIND ME, GUYS!
I'M JUST PASSING THROUGH!

128
00:05:21,059 --> 00:05:22,327
OKAY! YOU CAN CUT THAT OUT!

129
00:05:22,327 --> 00:05:24,262
I'M REALLY NOT TRYING
TO GET IN ANYBODY'S WAY!

130
00:05:25,897 --> 00:05:28,299
OH MY GOD!  WHY IS EVERYONE SO HOSTILE?!

131
00:05:30,168 --> 00:05:31,436
THIS THING'S SPINNING!

132
00:05:31,436 --> 00:05:32,570
I'M GETTING DIZZY!

133
00:05:33,104 --> 00:05:35,406
I CAN'T SHOOT YOU
ACCURATELY WHEN I'M DIZZY!

134
00:05:36,007 --> 00:05:36,808
WHERE ARE YOU?!

135
00:05:37,108 --> 00:05:37,775
NO!

136
00:05:40,445 --> 00:05:41,446
YOU FLANKING ME?

137
00:05:41,913 --> 00:05:44,182
I'M...READY...SORT OF!

138
00:05:46,217 --> 00:05:47,051
[exhales]

139
00:05:48,186 --> 00:05:51,022
I think I'm just going to
take a breather for a minute.

140
00:05:54,092 --> 00:05:55,734
I should've been a pirate.

